.TH WINCAN 5 "November 2026" "wincan" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
wincan.ini \- settings of wincan
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B %APPDATA%\\wincan\\wincan.ini
is a Windows INI file that the program writes when the window is moved and at exit.  It can be edited while the program is not running.
.SS [wincan]
.TP
.B server
.I HOST:PORT
of the candled server (default localhost:8766).
.TP
.B pair
the coin shown (default BTC).
.TP
.B tf
the timeframe: 1m 3m 5m 15m 30m 1h 4h 1d or 1w (default 5m).
.TP
.B scale
the size of the window in percent (75 to 400, default 100 = 300 by 175 pixels).
.TP
.B x, y
the position of the window on the screen (the top left corner of the screen the first time, and whenever hardly any of the window, less than 60 by 40 pixels, would be on a screen at the saved place; it may be partly off the screen).
.TP
.B editfield
the box (0 to 3) that e opens the position editor on: the one last edited.
.TP
.B bollinger, ma9, ma200
1 or 0: whether each indicator is drawn (default 1).
.TP
.B volcandles
1 or 0: whether the candles are drawn with a width in proportion to their volume (default 0: standard candles).
.SS [positions]
One line for each coin that has a position:
.I NAME=ENTRY,SIZE
with the entry price, the size in coins (negative for a short), the time opened (Unix seconds), the leverage and the realized profit or loss in dollars, for example
.BR BTC=61000,0.5,1795160000,10,15 .  The last three may be missing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wincan (1),
.BR candled (8)
